sentences.text:
Location: High Court of ...RESPONDENTS Karnataka  (BY SRI K. RAHUL RAI, HCGP FOR R-1;
 R-2 SERVED & UNREPRESENTED)
Nikhil vs State Of Karnataka on 12 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/103911351/

The petitioner is directed to be enlarged on bail in Spl.S.C.No.128/2024 pending before the Court of Additional District & Sessions Judge, FTSC-I, Chikkaballapura, arising out of Crime No.114/2024 registered by Chintamani Town Police, Station, Chikkaballapura District,
for the offences punishable under Sections 363, 366, 376 IPC, Sections 4, 12 & 17 of the POCSO Act,
2012, and Section 9 of the Prohibition of Child Marriage Act, 2006, subject to the following conditions:
Nikhil vs State Of Karnataka on 12 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/103911351/
3 a) Petitioner shall execute personal bond for a sum of Rs.1,00,000/- with two sureties for the likesum, to the satisfaction of the jurisdictional Court;
b) The petitioner shall appear regularly on all the dates of hearing before the Trial Court unless the Trial Court exempts his appearance for valid reasons;

c) The petitioner shall not directly or indirectly threaten or tamper with the prosecution witnesses;
d) The petitioner shall not involve in similar offences in future;
NC: 2024:KHC:51326 e) The petitioner shall not leave the jurisdiction of the Trial Court without permission of the said Court until the case registered against him is disposed off.

